      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "f0d391db9bf9ca39481477acf2acc4007c62a704",
            "subject": "LU-20211 mdt: trunc(0) layout replace on inactive stripes"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-02 20:26:10.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-03 01:49:20.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20211 lod: count offline OSTs to skip per-stripe checks",
        "message": "LU-20211 lod: count offline OSTs to skip per-stripe checks\n\nChecking a file for stripes on unavailable OSTs looks up the OST of\nevery stripe and its state, on every truncate (layout replace probe),\nFLR primary mirror pick and migration parent FID update, even though\nan OST is rarely unavailable.  A read-only OST was also treated as\nusable for truncate, so a truncate of a file with an object there\nwould fail with -EROFS instead of replacing that object.\n\nAdd lod_ost_offline_count, the number of OSTs that cannot modify\ntheir objects: the OSP import is not connected or is deactivated, or\nthe OST reported OS_STATFS_READONLY in its last statfs.  LOD gives\neach OST's OSP a pointer to the count with KEY_OFFLINE_COUNT when the\nOST is added, and clears it under ltd_mutex before the OST is\nremoved.  The OSP raises the count by one while it is unusable,\nchecked under a lock at each import event, read-only state change in\nosp_pre_update_msfs() and pointer change, so an OST that is offline\nwhen it is added is counted at once and a late IMP_EVENT_ACTIVE\ncannot undo a newer disconnect.  A connected OST that is full or not\nprecreating is not counted, since it can still be truncated and have\nits parent FID changed.\n\nSkip the per-stripe checks while the count is zero in\nlod_layout_check(MD_LAYOUT_UNAVAILABLE) and\nlod_obj_stripe_replace_parent_fid_offline_cb().  lod_ost_offline()\ntreats a read-only OST and an invalid (deactivated) import as\noffline, as the count does, reading the import and the OSP's cached\nstatfs rather than waiting for LOD's next statfs refresh.\n\nlod_primary_pick() must still avoid a mirror on any inactive OST, so\nit skips its check only while every OST is active, and takes each\nstripe's OST index from llc_ost_indices[] instead of an FLD lookup.\n\nWhile the checks are skipped, a stripe on an OST index that was\nremoved from the configuration is no longer reported unavailable.\n\nShow the count in lod.*.ost_offline_count, and add sanity/test_27xw\nto check that it rises when an OST is deactivated, stopped or made\nread-only and returns to zero afterward, that truncate(0) moves a\nfile off a read-only OST, and that a no-create OST is not counted.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-flr,sanity-ec\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I94d6b7e0b796824e00b3be87b2f036bc5d3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
